{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-1co-11-1","title":"1 Corinthians 11:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 He reproves them, because in holy assemblies, 4 their men prayed with their heads covered, 6 and women with their heads uncovered; 17 and because generally their meetings were not for the better, but for the worse; 21 as, namely, in profaning with their own feast the Lord's supper. 25 Lastly, he calls them to the first institution thereof.</p>\n<p>Be ye. 4:16; 10:33; Php 3:17; 1Th 1:6; 2Th 3:9; Heb 6:12 even. Ro 15:2,3; Eph 5:1,2; Php 2:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-2","title":"1 Corinthians 11:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>I praise. 17,22; Pr 31:28-31 that. 4:17; 15:2 keep. 7:17; Lu 1:6; 1Th 4:1,2; 2Th 2:15; 3:6 ordinances. or, traditions.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-3","title":"1 Corinthians 11:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the head of every. Eph 1:22,23; 4:15; 5:23; Php 2:10,11; Col 1:18; 2:10,19 and the head of the. Ge 3:16; Eph 5:22,24; Col 3:18; 1Ti 2:11,12; 1Pe 3:1,5,6 and the head of Christ. 3:23; 15:27,28; Isa 49:3-6; 52:13; 55:4; 61:1-4; Mt 28:18 Joh 3:34-36; 5:20-30; 14:28; 17:2-5; Eph 1:20-22; Php 2:7-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-4","title":"1 Corinthians 11:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>or. 12:10,28; 14:1-25 having. 14; 2Sa 15:30; 19:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-5","title":"1 Corinthians 11:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>or. Lu 2:36; Ac 2:17; 21:9 shaven. De 21:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-6","title":"1 Corinthians 11:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>but. Nu 5:18; De 22:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-7","title":"1 Corinthians 11:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>he is. Ge 1:26,27; 5:1; 9:6; Ps 8:6; Jas 3:9 but. 3; Ge 3:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-8","title":"1 Corinthians 11:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Ge 2:21,22; 1Ti 2:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-9","title":"1 Corinthians 11:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>the man. Ge 2:18,20,23,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-10","title":"1 Corinthians 11:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>power.That is, a covering in sign that she is under the power of her husband. [Exousia ,] appears here to be used for the sign or token of being under power or authority, that is, a veil, as Theophylact, (Ecumenius, and Photius) explain; and so one MS. of the Vulgate, the Sixtine edition, and some copies of the Itala, have {velamen.}</p>\n<p>Ge 20:16; 24:64,65 because. Ec 5:6; Mt 18:10; Heb 1:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-11","title":"1 Corinthians 11:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>7:10-14; 12:12-22; Ga 3:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-12","title":"1 Corinthians 11:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>but. 8:6; Pr 16:4; Ro 11:36; Heb 1:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-13","title":"1 Corinthians 11:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>10:15; Lu 12:57; Joh 7:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-14","title":"1 Corinthians 11:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>if. 2Sa 14:26 it is. 14:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-15","title":"1 Corinthians 11:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>covering. or, veil. 15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-16","title":"1 Corinthians 11:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>seem. 1Ti 6:3,4 such. Ac 21:21,24 the churches. 7:17; 14:33,34; 16:1; 1Th 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-17","title":"1 Corinthians 11:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>I praise. 2,22; Le 19:17; Pr 27:5; Ro 13:3; 1Pe 2:14 that ye. 20,34; 14:23,26; Isa 1:13,14; 58:1-4; Jer 7:9,10; Heb 10:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-18","title":"1 Corinthians 11:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>I hear. 1:10-12; 3:3; 5:1; 6:1 divisions. or, schisms. 1:10; 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-19","title":"1 Corinthians 11:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>there. Mt 18:7; Lu 17:1; Ac 20:30; 1Ti 4:1,2; 2Pe 2:1,2 heresies. or, sects. Ac 5:17; 15:5; 24:5,14; 26:5; 28:22; Ga 5:20; Tit 3:10; *Gr: which. De 13:3; Lu 2:35; 2Co 13:5-7; *Gr: 1Jo 2:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-20","title":"1 Corinthians 11:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>this is not to eat. or, ye cannot eat. 20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-21","title":"1 Corinthians 11:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>in. 23-25; 10:16-18 and one. 2Pe 2:13; Jude 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-22","title":"1 Corinthians 11:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>have. 34 or. 10:32; 15:9; Ac 20:28; 1Ti 3:5,15 that have not. or, that are poor. Pr 17:5; Jas 2:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-23","title":"1 Corinthians 11:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>I have. 15:3; De 4:5; Mt 28:20; Ga 1:1,11,12; 1Th 4:2 the same. Mt 26:2,17,34 took. Mt 26:26-28; Mr 14:22-24; Lu 22:19,20; Ac 20:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-24","title":"1 Corinthians 11:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>eat. 5:7,8; Ps 22:26,29; Pr 9:5; So 5:1; Isa 25:6; 55:1-3; Joh 6:53-58 this. 27,28; 10:3,4,16,17 in remembrance. or, for a remembrance. Ex 12:14; Jos 4:7; Ps 111:4; So 1:4; Isa 26:8; Mt 26:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-25","title":"1 Corinthians 11:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>This. 27,28 the new. Lu 22:20; 2Co 3:6,14; Heb 9:15-20; 13:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-26","title":"1 Corinthians 11:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>ye do shew. or, shew ye. till. 4:5; 15:23; Joh 14:3; 21:22; Ac 1:11; 1Th 4:16; 2Th 1:10; 2:2,3 Heb 9:28; 2Pe 3:10; 1Jo 2:28; Jude 1:14; Re 1:7; 20:11,12; 22:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-27","title":"1 Corinthians 11:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>whosoever. 10:21; Le 10:1-3; Nu 9:10,13; 2Ch 30:18-20; Mt 22:11 Joh 6:51,63,64; 13:18-27 shall be. 29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-28","title":"1 Corinthians 11:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>let a. 31; Ps 26:2-7; La 3:40; Hag 1:5,7; Zec 7:5-7; 2Co 13:5; Ga 6:4 1Jo 3:20,21 and so. Nu 9:10-13; Mt 5:23,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-29","title":"1 Corinthians 11:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>damnation. or, judgment.[Krima ,] judgment, or punishment, not damnation, for it was inflicted upon the disorderly and profane for their amendment.</p>\n<p>30,32-34; Ro 13:2; *Gr: Jas 3:1; 5:12; *marg: not. 24,27; Ec 8:5; Heb 5:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-30","title":"1 Corinthians 11:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>many. 32; Ex 15:26; Nu 20:12,24; 21:6-9; 2Sa 12:14-18; 1Ki 13:21-24 Ps 38:1-8; 78:30,31; 89:31-34; Am 3:2; Heb 12:5-11; Re 3:19 sleep. 15:51; Ac 13:36; 1Th 4:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-31","title":"1 Corinthians 11:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>28; Ps 32:3-5; Jer 31:18-20; Lu 15:18-20; 1Jo 1:9; Re 2:5; 3:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-32","title":"1 Corinthians 11:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>we are. 30; De 8:5; Job 5:17,18; 33:18-30; 34:31,32; Ps 94:12,13; 118:18 Pr 3:11,12; Isa 1:5; Jer 7:28; Zep 3:2; Heb 12:5-11 condemned. Ro 3:19; 1Jo 5:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-11-34","title":"1 Corinthians 11:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>if any. 21,22 condemnation. or, judgment. will I. 7:17; Tit 1:5 when. 4:19; 16:2,5</p>"}]}